# Shared, NON-SECRET defaults for every stack in this repo.
#
# This file IS committed. It is the source of truth in production too:
# Komodo passes it to `docker compose --env-file` via each Stack's
# `additional_env_files`. Anything sensitive belongs in Komodo's
# Variables & Secrets instead (see README.md) — never here.
#
# Local testing:
#   docker compose --env-file ../common.env --env-file prowlarr.env up

# --- Identity ---
PUID=1000
PGID=1000
TZ=Africa/Johannesburg

# --- Routing ---
# The tailnet-only half of the naming split (see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md):
# *.admin.jjventer.co.za is infrastructure, *.jjventer.co.za is public.
# Everything on pve-prod is admin-side for now — the ISP blocks inbound, so
# nothing here is publicly reachable regardless.
#
# Shared rather than Traefik-specific: Traefik uses it for the wildcard
# certificate and its own dashboard route, and every fronted service uses it
# in its Host rule. It started in traefik.env and moved here the moment a
# second stack needed it.
#
# One wildcard cert covers *.${ADMIN_DOMAIN} plus ${ADMIN_DOMAIN} itself.
# A wildcard covers exactly ONE label: prowlarr.admin.jjventer.co.za matches,
# a.b.admin.jjventer.co.za does not. Keep service hostnames flat.
#
# ⚠️ Docker labels substitute this; Traefik's FILE provider does NOT. Routes
# in stacks/platform/traefik/dynamic/*.yml therefore hardcode the domain and
# have to be edited by hand if this ever changes.
ADMIN_DOMAIN=admin.jjventer.co.za

# The LAN-reachable half. Added 2026-08-27.
#
# The two zones split on HOW A CLIENT REACHES pve-prod, not on trust:
#
#   *.admin.jjventer.co.za -> 100.91.183.47   pve-prod's tailnet address
#   *.home.jjventer.co.za  -> 10.42.0.11      pve-prod's LAN address
#
# Both names hit the same Traefik on the same host. AdGuard holds one rewrite
# per zone, so each name has exactly one answer everywhere.
#
# Why the admin zone moved to the tailnet address: pve-prod runs Tailscale in
# its own right, so pointing its names at a LAN address forced every client to
# carry the 10.42.0.0/24 subnet route. On jj-laptop that route collided with
# the physical path (Tailscale's policy table 52 is read before the main
# table), which is why --accept-routes had to be toggled per SSID. Addressing
# a Tailscale host by its tailnet address removes the toggle entirely.
#
# Use the home zone ONLY for services that devices without Tailscale must
# reach — a TV, a console, a guest laptop — and for bulk transfers where the
# WireGuard MTU and encryption cost is worth avoiding on a LAN.
#
# Two services carry a name in each zone: jellyfin and seerr. Both are used by
# people other than JJ, and those people are not on the tailnet. Everything
# else is single-operator and belongs in the admin zone only.
HOME_DOMAIN=home.jjventer.co.za

# --- Storage roots ---
# CONFIG_ROOT/<app> = each app's own settings/database, isolated per app.
# DATA_ROOT = ONE path mounted at /data identically in every *arr + download
# client container, so Radarr/Sonarr can hardlink/atomic-move files from the
# download client's folder into the media library instead of copying across
# a filesystem boundary. Do NOT give each app its own separate data subpath.
#
# The two roots are on DIFFERENT disks on purpose, as of 2026-08-03:
#   CONFIG_ROOT  /dev/sda1, the 64 GB VM root disk. Small, backed up.
#   DATA_ROOT    /dev/sdb,  a dedicated 1 TB LVM-thin volume mounted at
#                /mnt/data. Media only.
#
# DATA_ROOT used to sit under /mnt/docker-data on the root disk, which left
# 41 GB for the whole library and put the OS one season away from a full
# filesystem. The new disk is thin provisioned on pve's `local-lvm`, so
# pve-prod runs fstrim.timer — without discard the volume only ever grows
# and deleting media never returns space to the pool.
CONFIG_ROOT=/mnt/docker-data/appdata
DATA_ROOT=/mnt/data
